# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# nSelf Project Configuration
# Copy to .env and fill in your secrets.
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

PROJECT_NAME=myproject
BASE_DOMAIN=local.nself.org
ENV=dev

# Deploy target environment (local|staging|production). Used by `nself deploy`
# when --env is not passed on the command line. Defaults to production.
NSELF_DEPLOY_ENV=production

# Primary SSH key path for remote deploy (overrides NSELF_DEPLOY_SSH_KEY when set).
# NSELF_DEPLOY_KEY_PATH=~/.ssh/nself_deploy_ed25519

# Embedded PostgreSQL via pglite/wasmtime (no Docker postgres container).
# Set to true to activate; also pass --embedded-pg to `nself start`.
# When true, `nself build` omits the postgres Docker service and Hasura
# connects via a Unix-domain socket bridge. Requires CGO_ENABLED=1 build.
# NSELF_EMBEDDED_PG=

# NSELF_POSTGRES_MODE: runtime postgres path. Controls which Postgres backend
# nself uses when starting a stack.
#   docker  — standard Docker-managed Postgres container (default, fully supported)
#   wasm    — embedded pglite/wasmtime in-process Postgres (EXPERIMENTAL)
# The wasm path requires NSELF_EMBEDDED_PG=true and a CGO_ENABLED=1 build.
# The docker path is the primary supported runtime; the wasm path is opt-in only.
NSELF_POSTGRES_MODE=docker

POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
HASURA_GRAPHQL_ADMIN_SECRET=CHANGE_ME
HASURA_JWT_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# Prometheus metrics endpoint secret. Required when MONITORING_ENABLED=true.
HASURA_GRAPHQL_METRICS_SECRET=CHANGE_ME

# /healthz Hasura probe timeout in milliseconds (numeric, 1–29999, default 2000).
# When Hasura responds slower than this threshold, /healthz returns
# 200 {"status":"degraded","hasura":"slow"} instead of waiting indefinitely.
# Set lower (e.g. 500) in high-availability deployments where fast failover
# is preferred over tolerating slow upstream responses.
# HEALTHZ_HASURA_TIMEOUT_MS=2000

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Plugin: AI (nself-ai) — multi-provider LLM gateway
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# API key for inter-plugin authentication
# AI_API_KEY=

# Default AI provider: openai, anthropic, cohere, local
# AI_DEFAULT_PROVIDER=openai

# Default sampling temperature (0.0-2.0)
# AI_DEFAULT_TEMPERATURE=0.7

# Default max tokens per response
# AI_DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS=1000

# OpenAI API key (required when using openai provider)
# AI_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic API key (required when using anthropic provider)
# AI_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Enable local LLM (Ollama) — set base URL
# AI_LOCAL_ENABLED=false
# AI_LOCAL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434

# Per-user rate limiting (requests per minute)
# AI_RATE_LIMIT_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=60

# Per-user daily cost cap in USD
# AI_DEFAULT_DAILY_COST=10.00

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Gemini API keys — used by AI plugin tiered routing
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# Gemini Flash-Lite keys (tier 1, free, 60 RPM per key)
# Add multiple keys to increase effective rate limit.
# GEMINI_FREE_KEY_1=
# GEMINI_FREE_KEY_2=
# GEMINI_FREE_KEY_3=
# GEMINI_FREE_KEY_4=

# Gemini Flash keys (tier 2, paid Gemini Flash model, 40 RPM per key)
# GEMINI_FLASH_KEY_1=
# GEMINI_FLASH_KEY_2=

# Alias: treated as GEMINI_FREE_KEY_1
# AI_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Provider-level RPM limits for tiered routing
# PLUGIN_AI_GEMINI_FREE_RPM=60
# PLUGIN_AI_GEMINI_FLASH_RPM=40
# PLUGIN_AI_OPENAI_RPM=500
# PLUGIN_AI_ANTHROPIC_RPM=50
# PLUGIN_AI_OLLAMA_RPM=0

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Plugin: Claw (nself-claw) — AI personal assistant
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# Enable multi-user mode (default: false, single owner only)
# CLAW_MULTI_USER=false

# JWT secret for session tokens (generate with: openssl rand -hex 32)
# CLAW_JWT_SECRET=

# VAPID keys for web push notifications (auto-generated if not set)
# CLAW_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# CLAW_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# CLAW_VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:admin@example.com

# Shared secret between mux and claw plugins (generate with: openssl rand -hex 32)
# MUX_CLAW_SHARED_SECRET=

# Telegram bot integration
# CLAW_TG_BOT_TOKEN=
# CLAW_BASE_URL=
# CLAW_TG_ALLOWED_USERS=

# Allow shell command execution (security: review before enabling)
# NCLAW_ALLOW_SHELL=false

# Proactive intelligence (morning briefings, health alerts)
# NCLAW_PROACTIVE_ENABLED=false
# NCLAW_BRIEFING_TIME=08:00
# NCLAW_QUIET_START=22:00
# NCLAW_QUIET_END=08:00

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Redis (optional service — enable with REDIS_ENABLED=true)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# REDIS_ENABLED=false

# Redis image tag (default: 7-alpine)
# REDIS_VERSION=7-alpine

# Host port Redis binds to (default: 6379)
# REDIS_PORT=6379

# Optional password. When set, --requirepass and --protected-mode yes are injected.
# REDIS_PASSWORD=

# Memory limit for the Redis container (default: 512M)
# REDIS_MEMORY=512M

# CPU limit for the Redis container (default: 0.5)
# REDIS_CPU=0.5

# Maximum concurrent client connections passed to redis-server as --maxclients.
# Tune to match the sum of connection pool sizes across all services that connect
# to Redis (plugins, claw, queue workers, etc.).
# Default: 50 in prod environments, 20 in dev.
# REDIS_POOL_SIZE=50

# MeiliSearch warmup queries — comma-separated query strings run against each
# index on startup to pre-warm the cache. Optional; default empty (skip warmup).
# Example: MEILISEARCH_WARMUP_QUERIES=hello,world,search
# MEILISEARCH_WARMUP_QUERIES=

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# CLI operational env vars (nself binary)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# Command audit logging — records every CLI command for debugging.
# NSELF_CMD_LOG_ENABLED=true
# NSELF_CMD_LOG_MAX_SIZE_MB=10
# NSELF_CMD_LOG_KEEP_FILES=5
# The log is ~/.nself/logs/nself.log (directory 0700, files 0600). Secret
# arguments and flag values are written as [REDACTED]; URL passwords too.

# Health monitor — auto-restarts crashed services.
# NSELF_HEALTH_MAX_RESTARTS=5
# NSELF_HEALTH_POLL_INTERVAL=30s

# Profiling — pprof HTTP endpoint for CPU/memory profiling.
# NSELF_PPROF_BIND=127.0.0.1:6060
# NSELF_PROFILING_TOKEN=

# Pyroscope continuous profiling (optional).
# PYROSCOPE_ENABLED=false
# PYROSCOPE_SERVER_URL=http://pyroscope:4040
# PYROSCOPE_APPLICATION_NAME=nself-cli

# Watchdog escalation — alerts when health checks fail repeatedly.
# Telegram alerts:
# WATCHDOG_TG_BOT_TOKEN=
# WATCHDOG_TG_CHAT_ID=
# Email alerts (SMTP):
# WATCHDOG_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# WATCHDOG_SMTP_FROM=nself@example.com
# WATCHDOG_SMTP_USER=
# WATCHDOG_SMTP_PASS=

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Distributed Tracing — OpenTelemetry (H01)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# OTLP/gRPC exporter endpoint. Points at Tempo in the monitoring bundle.
# Override if Tempo runs on a different host/port.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4317

# Service name emitted on every span. Auto-set per plugin by InitTracing().
# Override only when running multiple instances behind a shared collector.
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=

# Sampling strategy. parentbased_traceidratio respects incoming trace decisions
# and applies the ratio to new root traces.
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=parentbased_traceidratio

# Sampling ratio: 1.0 = 100% (development default), 0.1 = 10% (production).
# Reduce to lower Tempo ingest volume at the cost of trace completeness.
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=1.0

# Log verbosity for the OTel SDK itself (not your application logs).
# Values: debug | info | warn | error. Default: warn.
# OTEL_LOG_LEVEL=warn

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Security & Retention (S44)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# Audit log retention window in days (default: 90, GDPR-aligned).
# Enterprise tier: 2555 (7 years). Business tier: 365 (1 year).
# AUDIT_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# Voice recording retention window in days (default: 90).
# REC_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# Maximum duration for a single RPi voice recording in seconds (default: 30).
# Hard cap: 3600 (1 hour). Prevents unbounded arecord resource consumption.
# RPI_MAX_RECORDING_SECONDS=30

# Allowed CORS origins for the claw plugin (comma-separated exact origins).
# Non-allowlisted origins with an Origin header are rejected with 403.
# Example: CLAW_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://claw.nself.org,https://app.nself.org
# CLAW_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# AI output moderation (S44-T08): URL of the moderation plugin service.
# When set, all AI completion output is checked through moderation/check before
# being returned to the caller. Fail-open: if unreachable, content passes through.
# Example: PLUGIN_MODERATION_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3715
# PLUGIN_MODERATION_INTERNAL_URL=

# Set to 1 to disable AI output moderation entirely (disables the modguard check).
# Default: unset (moderation ON when PLUGIN_MODERATION_INTERNAL_URL is set).
# Opt-out requires justification and security team sign-off.
# NSELF_AI_MODERATION_DISABLED=

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Cron Plugin — Env-Driven Schedule Bootstrap (G14-T02)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#
# Declare cron jobs as infrastructure-as-code. The cron plugin upserts these
# into Postgres on every container start, so schedules survive nself rebuild
# and server restarts without manual API calls.
#
# Format:
#   CRON_JOB_<N>_SCHEDULE  — Standard cron expression (required).
#   CRON_JOB_<N>_COMMAND   — HTTP callback URL that receives a POST on each tick (required).
#   CRON_JOB_<N>_NAME      — Display name for the job (optional; default: "env-job-<N>").
#   CRON_JOB_<N>_PAYLOAD   — JSON body sent with each POST (optional).
#
# N ranges 1..20. Gaps are fine (you can define 1, 2, 5 without filling 3 and 4).
# Jobs with the same name are updated in place when env vars change.
#
# Sample operator configs:
#
# --- Nightly Postgres backup to MinIO / S3 ---
# CRON_JOB_1_SCHEDULE=0 3 * * *
# CRON_JOB_1_COMMAND=http://backup:8080/backup/run
# CRON_JOB_1_NAME=nightly-pg-backup
#
# --- ICS feed regen (prayer times, events) ---
# CRON_JOB_2_SCHEDULE=0 0 * * *
# CRON_JOB_2_COMMAND=http://my-service:8080/tasks/regen-ics
# CRON_JOB_2_NAME=ics-regen
#
# --- Email digest dispatch via Elastic Email ---
# CRON_JOB_3_SCHEDULE=0 8 * * 1
# CRON_JOB_3_COMMAND=http://my-service:8080/tasks/email-digest
# CRON_JOB_3_NAME=weekly-email-digest
# CRON_JOB_3_PAYLOAD={"list":"subscribers","template":"weekly"}
#
# --- Hasura health probe ---
# CRON_JOB_4_SCHEDULE=*/5 * * * *
# CRON_JOB_4_COMMAND=http://hasura:8080/healthz
# CRON_JOB_4_NAME=hasura-health-probe

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Push Plugin — APNs + FCM (G14-T01)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#
# APNs (iOS): requires a .p8 auth key from developer.apple.com.
# Set PUSH_APNS_KEY_PEM to the raw PEM content (preferred for containers)
# or to a file path starting with "/" (file is read at container start).
#
# FCM (Android): requires a Firebase service account JSON.
# Set PUSH_FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON to the raw JSON content (preferred)
# or to a file path starting with "/" (file is read at container start).
#
# Neither, one, or both providers may be configured. The push service starts
# in degraded mode when credentials are absent and logs a clear warning.
#
# Credential rotation: update the env var and run `nself restart push`.
# The container reloads credentials from env on startup — no in-memory cache.

# APNs (iOS push notifications)
PUSH_APNS_TEAM_ID=
PUSH_APNS_KEY_ID=
PUSH_APNS_KEY_PEM=
PUSH_APNS_BUNDLE_ID=
# Set to 1 for APNs sandbox (development/staging); 0 or unset for production.
# PUSH_APNS_SANDBOX=0

# FCM (Android push notifications — v1 API, not legacy)
PUSH_FCM_PROJECT_ID=
PUSH_FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# Retry policy (optional — defaults shown)
# PUSH_RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# PUSH_RETRY_BACKOFF_BASE_MS=500
